cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PitchLens, please cite it as below."
title: "PitchLens: football analytics from broadcast video"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Inamdar
    given-names: Varun
    affiliation: Vishwakarma University, Pune, India
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/vnigoated/Football_Analytics"
abstract: >-
  Open pipeline from broadcast football video to player positions, roles and teams, and the code for the study of
  visibility bias in team pressing metrics: a broadcast camera fitted to real footprints, the bias experiments, a
  correction from the number of visible players, its validation on real video (SoccerNet-GSR, SportsMOT) and a
  main-camera filter for full broadcasts. Data are not included; they are downloaded from their original sources.
keywords:
  - football
  - soccer
  - broadcast tracking
  - pressing
  - measurement bias
  - computer vision
  - sports analytics
